{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1524806391,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMTgyODA3NDk=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2454","origin":"github"},"title":"`add` call triggered by `datalad run` cannot handle removed files","message":"Here is the minimal demo\n\n```\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/brkrun (git)-[master] % datalad add some\nadd(ok): /tmp/brkrun/some (file)\nsave(ok): /tmp/brkrun (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/brkrun (git)-[master] % datalad run git rm some\n[INFO   ] == Command start (output follows) ===== \nrm 'some'\n[INFO   ] == Command exit (modification check follows) ===== \nFailed to run ['git', '-c', 'receive.autogc=0', '-c', 'gc.auto=0', 'add', '--verbose', '--', 'some'] under '/tmp/brkrun'. Exit code=128. out= err=fatal: pathspec 'some' did not match any files\nfatal: pathspec 'some' did not match any files\n```\n\ninside `run` calls `add('.')`, which seems like the right thing to do -- although maybe it should be `save('.')`, going back to #2043 and #2428.\n\nApplying this diff\n\n```diff\n--- a/datalad/interface/run.py\n+++ b/datalad/interface/run.py\n@@ -223,5 +223,5 @@ def run_command(cmd, dataset=None, message=None, rerun_info=None):\n                  msg_path)\n         raise exc\n     else:\n-        for r in ds.add('.', recursive=True, message=msg):\n+        for r in ds.save(path='.', recursive=True, message=msg):\n             yield r\n```\n\nsolves the issue at hand (see example above), but breaks pretty much any existing `run` tests we have.","files":null}]}